WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
Your cells cannot make a single atom.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.640
Every nitrogen and phosphorus atom in
you was taken in from your surroundings.

3
00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.780
From those atoms come
four groups of molecules:

4
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.090
carbohydrates, lipids,
proteins and nucleic acids.

5
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:20.110
Many of them are giants, built by
joining small units again and again.

6
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.650
And every time a cell
builds one, water appears.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.250
Where does it come from?

8
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.900
In this mission, you'll meet
the small building blocks,

9
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:32.150
called monomers, and the long
chains they make, called polymers.

10
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.320
Then you'll watch the joining
reaction step by step,

11
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.970
and see how digestion pulls
big molecules apart again.

12
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.650
Your mission: find out why building
a big molecule always makes water.
